.SH "NAME"
cpmregistry \- command line interface for the CPM Registry REST API
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B cpmregistry
[\fIglobal options\fR] \fIcommand\fR [\fIsubcommand\fR] [\fIarguments\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
cpmregistry calls the CPM Registry REST API from the command line. Commands are grouped by resource, and every command prints its result to standard output in the configured format.
.PP
API for the CPM Registry, used by the Chung Package Manager (cpm) to host and distribute ComputerCraft\-focused Lua packages.
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-base\-url\fR \fI<url>\fR
Override the base URL for API requests.
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fI<ms>\fR
Request timeout in milliseconds.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-retries\fR \fI<count>\fR
Number of retries for retryable failures.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<format>\fR
Output format: auto, json, jsonl, pretty, raw, toon, yaml.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\-error\fR \fI<format>\fR
Error output format: auto, json, jsonl, pretty, raw, toon, yaml.
.TP
\fB\-\-transform\fR \fI<path>\fR
Dot\-path transform for data output.
.TP
\fB\-\-transform\-error\fR \fI<path>\fR
Dot\-path transform for error output.
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-raw\-output\fR
Print transformed string values without JSON quotes.
.TP
\fB\-\-debug\fR
Enable SDK debug logging on standard error.
.SH "COMMANDS"
.TP
\fBcpmregistry packages list\fR
List packages. See cpmregistry\-packages\-list(1).
.TP
\fBcpmregistry packages create\fR
Publish package version. See cpmregistry\-packages\-create(1).
.TP
\fBcpmregistry packages retrieve\fR
Get package. See cpmregistry\-packages\-retrieve(1).
.TP
\fBcpmregistry packages retrieve\-version\fR
Get package version. See cpmregistry\-packages\-retrieve\-version(1).
.TP
\fBcpmregistry packages resolve\fR
Resolve dependencies. See cpmregistry\-packages\-resolve(1).
.TP
\fBcpmregistry packages:dist list\-tarball\fR
Download tarball. See cpmregistry\-packages\-dist\-list\-tarball(1).
.TP
\fBcpmregistry packages:dist list\-bundle\fR
Download bundle. See cpmregistry\-packages\-dist\-list\-bundle(1).
.TP
\fBcpmregistry bootstrap list\-install\fR
Bootstrap installer. See cpmregistry\-bootstrap\-list\-install(1).
.TP
\fBcpmregistry completion\fR
Print a shell completion script. See cpmregistry\-completion(1).
.SH "SHELL COMPLETION"
cpmregistry completion <shell> prints a completion script for bash, zsh, and fish. Load it from your shell startup file:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
eval "$(cpmregistry completion bash)"
eval "$(cpmregistry completion zsh)"
cpmregistry completion fish | source
.fi
.RE
